From: mscharged-port
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve Wii32 audio arena size declaration in native builds
Upstream-base: 8b0505a47990d684d1588749f40babb9c0483490

AudioBackend.cpp already defines gAudioMemorySize as u32. Native unsigned long
is64 bits, so use the same32-bit type at the declaration. Original requests,
allocation sizes and all AudioBackend bodies remain unchanged. This does not
construct or initialize the original backend, AX, DSP or any audio effect.

diff --git a/include/Game/Audio/AudioGlobals.h b/include/Game/Audio/AudioGlobals.h
--- a/include/Game/Audio/AudioGlobals.h
+++ b/include/Game/Audio/AudioGlobals.h
@@ -16,7 +16,11 @@
 extern AudioSystem* g_pAudioSystem;
 extern AudioBackend* g_pAudioBackend;
 extern void* g_pAudioSilenceBuffer;
+#ifdef MSCHARGED_NATIVE
+extern u32 gAudioMemorySize;
+#else
 extern unsigned long gAudioMemorySize;
+#endif
 extern unsigned int gResidentVoiceDropCount;
 extern unsigned int gStreamVoiceDropCount;
 
